/-!
# The U₅(4) plane residual, its canonical two-core and quotient

The full plane parabolic has a faithful unipotent matrix subgroup and a Levi
quotient GL₂(F₁₆) modulo scalar fifth roots. The unipotent--SL₂ subgroup is
perfect and has abelian quotient of order three in the parabolic, identifying
it with the actual solvable residual. Its canonical two-core is the constructed
unipotent subgroup, has order `2^16`, and has quotient PSL₂(F₁₆).

This module also re-exports the index seventeen of the literal flag overlap
in the plane parabolic. The two-parabolic Sylow marking and final source
amalgam assembly remain with their respective consumers.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
F.1.12(7), printed pp.263--264.
-/
